title: All Butter Pie Crust

---

## Ingredients (for 1 12" crust)
* 150g all-purpose flour
* 1/2 tsp salt
* 1/2 block unsalted butter, about 120g
* 3 - 6 tbsp cold water, about 45-90g

## Instructions

1. Grate 30g of the butter. Set aside in the freezer.
2. Cut remaining butter into 1 inch cubes.
3. In a food processor, pulse 90g flour, salt and cubed butter.
4. Break up the dough, and add the rest of the flour and pulse again.
5. In a large bowl, combine dough with the butter shreds and water. Start with 3tbsp of water, add more only if necessary.
6. Wrap the dough with plastic wrap in the shape of a flat disk.
7. Chill dough in fridge for at least an hour.

## To Use
1. Let the dough warm up for 10-15 min on the counter, so that it is malleable.
2. Flour the counter and roll the dough out.
3. Tuck it into the baking dish gently. Don't press it in.
